WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:04.580
It can't be easy for George Lucas to sit back
and watch other filmmakers guide the Star

00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:05.320
Wars galaxy.

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:09.100
Of course, it's hard to know for sure because
he doesn't seem to say a lot on the subject

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:09.600
lately.

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:14.500
Lucas has not been directly involved in the
franchise since it was sold to Disney in 2012,

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:18.700
but he seems to approve of the direction,
even if his words on the subject are few and

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:19.360
far between.

00:00:19.730 --> 00:00:22.540
Back when The Force Awakens arrived, Lucas
told Vulture that:

00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:23.680
… "fans are going to love it"...

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:24.960
and that it was:

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:27.200
"very much the kind of movie they’ve been
looking for."

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:31.520
Some perceived his word choice as a backhanded
compliment, but he had a similar response

00:00:31.539 --> 00:00:36.480
to Rogue One, as director Gareth Edwards said
in a press conference that Lucas "really liked"

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:37.280
the anthology flick.

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:41.640
And just days ahead of the release of The
Last Jedi, too, the originator of the Star

00:00:41.649 --> 00:00:46.260
Wars universe had a similar reaction to the
flick written and directed by Rian Johnson

00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:50.770
-- with his representatives telling The Hollywood
Reporter that he thought the movie was "beautifully

00:00:50.770 --> 00:00:54.180
made," and that he was "complimentary" to
Johnson after seeing it.

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:57.880
Johnson had previously said that while he
was attempting to pursue his own vision of

00:00:57.880 --> 00:01:02.240
the story, he wanted it to still be something
that would satisfy long-time fans by offering:

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:05.800
"Some things we haven't seen in Star Wars
before.

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:09.140
And hopefully it still feels like a Star Wars
movie, that's the number one thing."

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:13.860
For Johnson, making a Star Wars movie meant
keeping it light-hearted, despite the intensity.

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:19.500
"I think, I hope fans are gonna be pleasantly
surprised by how fun and funny this movie

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:20.000
is."

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:24.980
As of now, The Last Jedi has a 93 percent
fresh rating on Rotten Tomatoes, which makes

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:28.280
it the best-rated Star Wars flick on the aggregator.

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:32.520
And while some viewers have knocked the movie's
audience score down to well below that figure,

00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:37.350
it's clear The Last Jedi has at least offered
enough suspense and surprises to satisfy those

00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:39.680
who matter most, including George Lucas.

00:01:39.980 --> 00:01:40.860
Thanks for watching!

